;; str-vector-operand.toc
;;
;; Regression test: a Vector operand in a multi-operand concatenation
;; (`str` or `println`) is silently dropped, and the whole expression
;; vanishes -- the println below emits NO line at all (only START and
;; END appear in the .rslt).
;;
;; Per docs/toccata-style.md, a multi-operand string concatenation whose
;; operand is a Vector should render the vector with `[ ]` and
;; space-joined elements. Instead the vector operand -- and the entire
;; concatenation -- is erased by codegen. The trigger is the
;; multi-operand concatenation itself, not `str` specifically: passing
;; the vector operand straight to `println` (as below) vanishes too.
;;
;; Correct output would include the line:  VEC:[defn]
;; Buggy output (current .rslt):           that line is absent.
;;
;; This is the root cause of the intrp-emit.toc All/Concat render
;; failure (parser-generator-plan item 4b.3): the String render-child
;; impl returns a vector, and folding it into a multi-operand str or
;; println yields nothing, so every render result that passes through
;; such a concatenation comes back empty.

(main [argv]
  (println "START")
  (println "VEC:[" (vec "defn") "]")
  (println "END"))
